*.log
.DS_Store
# `.env` on its own matches only that exact name, so a root `.env.local` or
# `.env.production` was never ignored. site/.gitignore already used `.env*`;
# the root was the half that could still commit a key.
.env*
.parked/
CLAUDE.md
HISTORY.md
node_modules/
rabadon-study-notlar/
referans/
study/
BUGUN-*.md
# .rabadon/ holds two different things: live per-machine session state, and the
# guard this repo enforces on ITSELF. Ignoring the directory hid both, so
# guard_lint_test.sh's "this repo's own guard.json lints clean" arm passed here
# and died in every clean clone. Ignore the contents, re-include only the guard.
# `.rabadon/` (whole directory) would make the negation a no-op: git never
# descends into an excluded directory, so a file inside cannot be un-ignored.
# The glob must stay `**/.rabadon/*`, not `.rabadon/*`: a pattern with a slash
# in it anchors to this file's directory, which would un-ignore the nested
# native/.rabadon, site/.rabadon and reports/*/.rabadon — each of which holds
# its own state.json/handoff.md. The negation IS anchored, on purpose: only the
# root guard is shipped, nested ones stay local.
**/.rabadon/*
!/.rabadon/guard.json
# promise.json is the target rabadon-drift measures every session against, and
# leaving it untracked meant there was no way to reconstruct what the target
# said on any given day. On 2 August a supervised session had put the two rules
# protecting this file into disabled[], and the drift check then answered "on
# the star" for eight days against a promise the drifter could rewrite. The
# rules are sealed in the binary now; the history belongs here so that a moved
# north star shows up in a diff like every other change. The file carries no
# secrets, only the star, the areas, the anti-paths and the vocabulary.
!/.rabadon/promise.json
# built binaries — the source is the artifact, not the a.out. Every
# rabadon-<name> executable, never the .cpp/.h/.sh that make them.
native/rabadon-*
!native/rabadon-*.cpp
!native/rabadon-*.h
!native/rabadon-*.sh
*.o

# platform packages carry binaries only in CI (copied in before publish),
# never committed — the package.json/README templates ARE committed.
npm/*/rabadon-*

# npm pack output
*.tgz

# the micro benchmark is a built binary like the rest; the source is the artifact
native/gate_bench

.rabadon/state.json
.rabadon/handoff.md

# `rabadon init` writes .claude/settings.json into the project it is setting up,
# and the hook commands in it are ABSOLUTE paths on this machine — seven of
# them, account name included. It arrived untracked and unignored, so one
# `git add -A` by any session in this repository would have published the
# operator's home path in the tool that exists to stop exactly that.
.claude/

# python bytecode from site/build.py and its imports
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# editor and OS leftovers. None of these were ignored, so a stray swap file or
# an .idea/ directory from opening the tree in another editor would have shown
# up as untracked noise in every `git status` and been easy to sweep in.
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.idea/
.vscode/
._*
